    {
      "id": "WDL-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "A unimodular Gram fibre has the same normalized density at every positive level",
      "anchor": "lifts-whittaker-density",
      "statement": "At a good finite place with base residue size q, for 1≤n≤M and unimodular Hermitian J,T, the density is the product over 0≤j<n of (1−(ε/q)^(M−j)). Each solution modulo ϖᵏ lifts to q^(2Mn−n²) solutions modulo ϖ^(k+1) for k≥1.",
      "hypotheses": "Unramified quadratic valuation algebra over the local base, ε=−1 in the field case and +1 in the split case, Hermitian source and target of ranks M and n with invertible determinants. The application uses good odd places and the integral matrix-lattice test. The lifting demonstration with division by 2 uses this odd-place hypothesis.",
      "equations": [
        "lifts-whittaker-level"
      ],
