    {
      "id": "WDL-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "Finite Fourier interpolation computes the good Whittaker integral",
      "anchor": "lifts-whittaker-analytic",
      "statement": "The good-place integral equals ∏_{j=0}^{n−1}(1−ε^(M+j)q^(−(2z+n−j))) for Re(z)>n². This expression extends holomorphically to all z, and its value at z₀=(M−n)/2 is the density in WDL-01.",
      "hypotheses": "Good local data include an integral trace-self-dual lattice, unramified quadratic algebra, unit 2, character of valuation-ring conductor, integral unimodular J and T, and the standard lattice indicator. Both Fourier measures are self-dual for their prescribed pairings. The auxiliary lattice height is vol(L+bL)/vol(L) and appears to the power −(z−z₀).",
      "equations": [
        "lifts-whittaker-integral",
        "lifts-whittaker-good-factor"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "WDL-01"
      ],
