      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "The Gram character is positive and the target character is negative. In the quotient by integral Hermitian matrices the sum at each positive level is computed by polynomial interpolation at (ε/q)^m, m≥n, using finite orthogonality and the Gram density for the identity form. A uniform geometric bound justifies passage to the full integral on the right half-plane. Its continuation supplies the stated value at the target point.",
