    {
      "id": "WDL-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "The good factors enter the global full-rank coefficient through a separate density-to-mean identity",
      "anchor": "lifts-whittaker-assembly",
      "statement": "In the strict-rank case the product of the real factor, finitely many exceptional finite factors, and the good-place product agrees with the global Whittaker family sufficiently far right. The continued global value at z₀ is the normalized rational Gram-fibre mean by the low-rank global density theorem.",
